    <!-- Help. -->
    <string name="help_title">How to play</string>
    <string name="help_goal_title">The goal</string>
    <string name="help_goal">Beat the dealer\'s hand without going over 21. Number cards count their number, face cards count 10, and an Ace counts 1 or 11, whichever is better. An Ace and a ten-value card on the first two cards is Blackjack, and pays 3 to 2. The dealer always stands on 17 or more, including soft 17.</string>
    <string name="help_decisions_title">Your decisions</string>
    <string name="help_decisions">Hit takes a card; Stand keeps your hand. Double, on your first two cards, doubles your bet and takes exactly one more card. Split, on two cards of the same rank, makes two hands, up to four in all; split Aces get one card each. When the dealer shows an Ace you may take insurance for half your bet: it pays 2 to 1 if the dealer has Blackjack. Every round is dealt from a fresh shuffle, and there is no undo.</string>
    <string name="help_chips_title">Chips</string>
    <string name="help_chips">You start with 1,000 chips. Chips are for play only and cannot be bought or cashed out. Bets go in steps of 10, from 10 up to 500. If you run out of chips you can reset to 1,000, and your statistics are kept.</string>
